        "text": "ment into the production server).\nI\nI Manual code review is essential because an automated tool is not enough\nto cover 100 percent of the source code. After finishing a new feature (by\nthe dev), you must go through this step.\nI\nI Most of the time, the source code uses open source third-party libraries\n(the goal is to add more functionalities to the application). In this case,\nit\u2019s your duty to check for these three items:\nI\nI Is the library containing any vulnerabilities?\nI\nI Is it up-to-date?\nI\nI Is it legal to use it for commercial use?\nClient\nData Flow Diagram\nAdmin\nWeb API\nData Store\nWebsite\nFigure 9.24: Data Flow Diagram\nChapter 9 I Web Penetration Testing and Secure Software\n255\nTo get the job done, there are automated scanners (e.g., Sonatype Lifecycle)\nthat can check these three items.",
